{
 "gdd": "in-world-instruments-and-inspect-view",
 "blocking": [
  "Detailed Rules IW-11(e), IW-12, IW-13 dispatch table (L272-274), S2 FILTER_DRIVEN row (L518); Interactions I-A; Formulas D.5 Output Range; E-IW-33, E-IW-35; AC-IW-19, -20, -44, -69 (vs perception-filter.md PF-8 L269-270, PF-17 L349, motion-state L554; registry L1411): [main review, confirmed by creative-director] The Instruments GDD never mentions the Filter's tenth Perceived field tremor_weight_pm or the BREATH motion_mode (grep finds 0 hits). The Filter is the publisher and the registry source. PF-8 L270 and PF-17 L349 say an honest tremor that is running at lie onset is blended out over TREMOR_BLEND_S := WANDER_ONSET_S, not stopped. PF L335/L554 send BREATH for static-pair frames, and registry L1411 records the amendment. IW S2 L518 says instead 'triple, tremor and notch cleared that frame', and the IW-13 dispatch table has no BREATH row. AC-IW-20/69 contradict AC-PF-46/85 at the same interface, so both test suites cannot pass. G1 says the publisher wins. This also matters for feel: a tremor that stops dead at lie onset is itself a tell, which is the opposite of what the Filter's onset rule is for. FIX: Add tremor_weight_pm to I-A and IW-5. Define the drawn tremor as round(TREMOR_GAIN x A_eff x env x s x tremor_weight_pm/1000), clamped as in D.5. Reword IW-11(e), IW-12, S2 and the D.5 Output Range to say: no NEW tremor starts in a non-HONEST frame; a tremor already running fades by tremor_weight_pm; the offset is 0 once the weight is 0. Keep the clearing of the reduced-motion notch and of the settle triple immediate, and say so explicitly. Add a BREATH row to IW-13 and S2: frame_override held still, the gleam breathes via leak_amplitude_pm, no needle motion, no settle, no tremor. Rewrite AC-IW-20, -44, -69 and E-IW-33/35 to match, and add AC-IW-19 legs for BREATH and for the tremor fade."
 ]
}
